    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate on June 21, the Austin Waves offense is anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (77.24) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.96), who both benefit from favorable matchups against Young. **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable asset, with the SP matchup against a 4.79 xERA providing an elite foundation for production, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leverages a strong dynamic platoon advantage and a premium #2 lineup slot to maximize his efficiency. **Andy Pages** (71.38) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.07) round out our top-tier plays, both capitalizing on weak opposing pitching\u2014Gasser\u2019s 5.06 xERA makes **Drake Baldwin** a high-upside start behind the dish, while **Andy Pages** continues to demonstrate the consistent contact quality required for a 90-plus efficiency ceiling.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nasim Nunez**, who registered a 49.49 score. While **Nasim Nunez** offers the elite sprint speed we covet for our stolen base deficit, he was ultimately benched due to a sub-optimal #9 batting order position and a perceived lower projected efficiency compared to the starting nine. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) earned his spot in the lead-off position largely due to his strong xwOBA profile and the favorable matchup against Montero, providing us with a high-floor spark at the top of the order. Meanwhile, **Coby Mayo** (37.85) fell below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" and was excluded to preserve our game caps, as his matchup against the 3.34 xERA of Sheehan presents too much risk for limited expected return. Keep a close eye on the weather and official lineups, particularly for **Jackson Merrill**, whose 57.31 projection is suppressed by Eovaldi\u2019s ability to limit base-stealing opportunities, making him the most sensitive play if the game environment shifts.",
